A||||13||b_b_a_d||NOS???||||5||
Z||000000||b_b_a_d||02-23-2000||01:30 AM||||Has anyone added nos to their car?  If so, which kit did you put on and were you happy with the outcome?  I was looking at a single stage 75-150 HP kit made for GM's EFI cars.  Any info would be appreciated!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||5
Z||000001||FIEROCIOUS||02-23-2000||04:51 AM||||Thats a excellent choice! Remember to mount the nitrous nozzle as far away from the trottle body as you can while keeping it in the air flow. (This adds power by super cooling the air and fully mixing the nitrous) Also don't get HP crazy stop at 75 shot deffinatly no more than a 100 shot! Before you do it call NOS and get their book! It has tons of info! ||||reg||1
Z||000002||87 Steve GT||02-23-2000||07:15 AM||||Is there any good webpages telling more about NOS ???  Is the NOS unit hard to install??                  Steve....||||reg||1
Z||000003||87 Steve GT||02-23-2000||07:23 AM||||I mean is it hard to install in on our 2.8??||||reg||1
Z||000004||Wrench||02-23-2000||07:40 PM||||Been running NOS on my '86 GT since '90 with zero problems. Just use common sense. I limit my bursts to WOT and just long enough to dust off the competetion. Piece of cake to install. Have fun and don't laugh to loud, and watch the competetion dissappear in your mirror. Follow NOS suggestions and you will do fine!!||||reg||14
Z||000005||b_b_a_d||02-23-2000||11:59 PM|||| <A HREF="http://www.nosnitrous.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.nosnitrous.com/</A> <P>There are a few interesting tips and some basic info at the NOS websight.  It will probably be a month or so before I actually do this, but I will keep you posted as things progress.||||reg||1
Z||000007||1FST2M6||02-24-2000||01:18 AM||||a past topic that just happens to be right up your alley.. MINE TOO! Happy Tire Smoking! I love my car with nitrous. might also want to talk to Shaun1178@aol.com  heres a post of my latest Dyno runs and shaun has his on his web site.  <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/002121.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/002121.html</A>   <A HREF="http://www.engineered.net/fiero.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.engineered.net/fiero.htm</A>  <A HREF="http://members.aol.com/shaun41178/" TARGET=_blank>http://members.aol.com/shaun41178/</A>  <p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 02-24-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||1FST2M6||02-24-2000||03:00 PM||||oh for those of you that went to the engineered fiero page.. I'm not really trying to sell her any more... but everthing has its price. To many Sudden acceleration and Fast driving awards forced me to want to sell her for about 4 months.. well the nice judge said i can keep my liscense so I'm keeping her for now.. unless some one has a White Fastback Automatic they'd like to trade!  ||||reg||1
Z||000009||1FST2M6||02-24-2000||03:17 PM||||As for how hard it is to put on.. The first kit i put on took me about 9 hours.. (hidding all the wires and grommeting all the holes and making it all pretty..) well I can do the same thing now in about 4. Its VERY straight forward. But i reccomend getting either the supplied hose shortend or buying a shorter one. The one supplied in the kit Part# 05120  has a 6' long tube... thats WAY to long.. I bought one thats only 18" and that made a noticable difference in responce time.. plus with the shorter tube I don't need a cheesy purge kit... nitrous is expensive and thats seems like a waste to me. I just wish there was room in the<BR> trunk for a remote bottle valve... I've toyed around with it but just can't find a way to mount it and not have it in the way more than this HUGE bottle already is... Everyone needs nitrous! I've had/have it on 5 cars and only killed one... cause i didn't install it right... make sure you read ALL the instructions and if you have ANY questions call the guys at either NOS or Nitrous Works they'll be more than happy to help you! And make sure your injectors are working properly. The more fuel you get to the combustion chamber the better off you'll be. ||||reg||1
Z||000010||DRH||02-24-2000||03:58 PM||||1FST2M6, Would it be correct to say that NOS has been harder on your driving record than your cars???||||reg||12
Z||000011||1FST2M6||02-24-2000||04:20 PM||||HEHE!!! your probly right.. my girlfriend says the same thing...    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">   ||||reg||1
Z||000012||1FST2M6||02-24-2000||04:28 PM||||OH yeah... before you go buying your nitrous kit or poly bushings you might want to try other store besides the Fiero store. they seem rather steep in their pricing. I got Poly Cradle bushing set from NOPI for $42 including shipping... much less than the $70 advertised. As for the nitrous kit. well at the time i worked at nopi so it was REALLY cheap but it retails for like $470 or so... #05120 and expect to be investing in new jets.. luckily thier cheap. $1.95!! cheapest hp increase i've EVER had! from the weak 70hp shot little changing some stuff and 2 jets later granted i lost HP but gained  just GOBS and GOBS of torque. HP makes you fast Torque make you quick... <A HREF="http://www.nopi.com" TARGET=_blank>www.nopi.com</A>  and another place where i all got my stuff  <A HREF="http://www.engineered.net" TARGET=_blank>www.engineered.net</A>  ||||reg||1
Z||000013||Capt Fiero||02-24-2000||08:30 PM||||With all the talk about nos, with nos you need more gas, has anyone thought of connecting the cold start injector up to the nos relay so when you hit the nos at W/O/T it will give you that extra hit of gas with it.||||reg||10
Z||000014||1FST2M6||02-24-2000||08:36 PM||||COOL IDEA!!! humm  i'll make some phone calls...  damn thats a good idea.. ||||reg||1
